    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We can use the tangent subtraction formula to solve this problem.\n\\begin{align*}\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) &= \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\tan x + 1}{1 - \\tan x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{-3}\n\\end{align*}\nOr, we can use the angle addition formula for tangent.\n\\begin{align*}\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) &= \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\tan x + 1}{1 - \\tan x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{-3}\n\\end{align*}\nThus, the value of $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)$ is $-3.$",
