    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find \\(\\tan\\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\) given that \\(\\tan x = 2\\), we can use the tangent addition formula. The formula for the tangent of a sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\tan (A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\n\nIn our problem, \\(A = x\\) and \\(B = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\). We know \\(\\tan x = 2\\) and \\(\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(\\tan x = 2\\) and \\(\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\\):\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{1 - 2} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
